  "manual": "GLOSSARY. **Spell Counter** = a token most cards in this deck bank each time a Spell resolves; nearly every Endymion/Mythical Beast Pendulum gains 1 (Jackal King and Master Cerberus gain 2) whenever ANY Spell resolves — yours or the opponent's. Counters are the deck's currency: you spend them to Special Summon, negate, banish, and destroy. **Scale / Pendulum Zone** = the two side zones; put a Pendulum monster in each and you may once per turn Pendulum Summon monsters whose Level is strictly between the two scale numbers, from hand and from face-up Pendulum monsters in your Extra Deck. **Face-up in the Extra Deck** = when a Pendulum monster would leave the field it lands face-up in the Extra Deck, where Magister of Endymion and Jackal King can re-summon it.\n\n=== BIG PICTURE ===\nYou are a combo/control Spellcaster deck. You play a wall of cantrip Spells (3x Upstart Goblin, 3x Into the Void, Pot of Desires, the Spellbook mini-engine) whose ONLY real purpose is to make Spell Counters pile onto your Pendulum monsters and onto Magical Citadel / Mythical Institution. Once counters are stacked you convert them into a Special-Summon chain that ends on **Endymion, the Mighty Master of Magic** as an omni-negate boss, backed by **Mythical Beast Jackal King** (monster-effect negate) and **Master Cerberus** (effect-destruction-immune 2800 beater with a banish). Citadel and Institution redirect destruction to counter-removal, so the board is very hard to break by popping.\n\n=== THE ENGINE PIECES ===\n- **Spell Power Mastery (3, your best starter):** adds ANY 'Endymion' card from Deck (grab Endymion the boss, or a Servant/Magister, or Magical Citadel), and places Spell Counters equal to how many Spell Power Mastery you control/GY (ramps as you play more copies). This one card is your search + your first counters.\n- **Servant of Endymion (3):** in a Pendulum Zone it gains a counter per Spell; remove 3 counters to Special Summon ITSELF from the zone PLUS any 1000+ ATK counter-holder from Deck (fetch Master Cerberus / Jackal King / another Endymion). Its monster effect: once per opponent's turn discard 1 to place a counter on every card you control that can hold one — mass-loads counters before an Endymion wipe or to arm negates.\n- **Magister of Endymion (2):** remove 3 counters to SS itself from the zone + revive 1 face-up monster from your Extra Deck; and once per opponent's turn remove 3 counters to SS a counter-holder from Deck (on-turn disruption/extension).\n- **Reflection of Endymion (1):** remove 3 counters to SS itself + a monster from HAND; on Special Summon it bounces 1 opponent card AND 1 of your own counter-cards, re-banking the counters — a free interruption that recycles.\n- **Mythical Beast Jackal (2, Level 1):** Pendulum effect self-destructs to seed a counter; monster effect removes 3 counters + tributes itself to SS a 'Mythical Beast' from Deck (tutor Jackal King / Master Cerberus / Bashilisk / Garuda). Being Level 1 it feeds Linkuriboh, Relinquished Anima, and Artemis.\n- **Mythical Beast Master Cerberus (1, Level 8 / 2800):** Pendulum effect self-destructs to ADD a Lv7-or-lower Mythical Beast from Deck; monster effect is immune to effect destruction while 4+ counters sit on your field, and removes 4 counters to banish an opponent monster and steal its ATK.\n- **Mythical Beast Jackal King (3):** on-board negate — banks 2 counters per Spell and, once per turn, removes 2 counters to negate+destroy an opponent's monster effect. Its Pendulum effect self-destructs to revive a Mythical Beast Pendulum from the Extra Deck. Three copies = layered negates.\n- **Magical Abductor (1):** counter monster; remove 3 to add a Pendulum from Deck, or a Level-1 Spellcaster.\n- **Mythical Beast Bashilisk (1):** Pendulum effect recycles a Spellcaster Pendulum from ED into the Deck AND draws 1; monster effect bounces a Mythical Beast back to hand.\n- **Mythical Beast Garuda (1):** Pendulum effect destroys another S/T (and itself); monster effect is a soft handtrap — when the opponent summons, remove 3 counters to SS itself from hand and bounce their monster.\n- **Field/Continuous banks:** **Magical Citadel of Endymion (2)** stores counters, lets you pay counter-costs from it, and survives destruction by removing 1 counter. **Mythical Institution (3)** is a Level-based tutor (remove N counters -> add a counter-holder of Level N from Deck or face-up ED) that also tanks destruction. **Mythical Bestiary (1)** mills 2 and places up to 2 counters; if destroyed it Special Summons a counter-holder from Deck.\n- **Spellbook mini-engine:** Spellbook Magician of Prophecy searches Spellbook of Secrets -> Spellbook of Knowledge (dump a Spellcaster or Spellbook, draw 2). Extra Spell activations = extra counters, and it fuels **Crowley, the First Propheseer** in the Extra Deck.\n- **Magia Magic - Thunder of Judgment (1):** a Magistus/Endymion Spell — pay a Magistus or 2 counters to EITHER Special Summon a Spellcaster from hand/face-up ED/GY, OR banish 1 card on the field. Flexible extender + spot removal, and pairs with Artemis (Magistus) in the Extra Deck.\n\n=== A TYPICAL GOING-FIRST LINE ===\n1) Resolve Spell Power Mastery: search Endymion the boss (or a missing piece) and bank your first counters. 2) Chain cheap Spells (Upstart, Into the Void once you hold 3+, Pot of Desires, the Spellbooks) to flood counters onto a Servant/Magister set in a Pendulum Zone and onto Citadel/Institution. 3) Spend counters: Servant SS's itself + a Deck monster; Magister revives from the Extra Deck; Jackal tutors a Mythical Beast; you build to **Heavymetalfoes Electrumite** (2 Pendulum monsters -> on summon add a Pendulum from Deck to your Extra Deck FACE-UP; then destroy your own scale to add a face-up Extra Deck Pendulum to HAND, which also draws you 1) and then **Selene, Queen of the Master Magicians** (banks counters on summon, then removes 3 to revive a Spellcaster in Defence Position). 4) Set the endboard: put **Endymion** in a Pendulum Zone or the Monster Zone (his Pendulum effect removes 6 counters to SS himself and destroy up to as-many-cards-as-you-control-that-hold-counters). Leave counters banked so Endymion has one (targeting- and destruction-immune) and Jackal King(s) can negate. Optionally hold **I:P Masquerena** to make **S:P Little Knight** (banish disruption) on the opponent's turn.\n\nENDBOARD (ideal): Endymion (Quick-Effect omni-negate: bounce your own counter-card to negate+destroy anything, protected while he holds a counter) + 1-2 Jackal King (monster-effect negate, 2 counters each) + Master Cerberus (effect-destruction-immune 2800, banish) + Magical Citadel + Mythical Institution banking counters, with S:P Little Knight as extra interruption from I:P Masquerena (NOT Apollousa — see EXTRA DECK).\n\n=== EXTRA DECK ===\nEvery slot, sourced. Tags: [S] = Shadow Spector's own words — his written 'Notes & Combos' on the Master Duel Meta page this list was copied from, plus auto-captioned transcripts of his streams and Q&A appearances. [MDM] = Master Duel Meta's In-Depth Endymion Guide (Gecko-chan & Lord Vectra). [LC] = Literature-chan's Endymion guides (MightyCitadel; TCG/OCG/Master Duel editions). [DATA] = copy counts tallied from Master Duel Meta's public top-deck API across 100 Endymion top decks. UNSOURCED means no player source justifies that slot — treat it as a spare body, not a plan.\n\nTHE LINE, VERBATIM [S]: \"The basic essence of the strategy is to use Servant to summon a negate (Jackal King or Endymion) from the deck. Then go into Electrumite to pull another negate from the deck. Use Electrumite to pop any pendulums in your hand to to fix your scales (pop a low scale [scale 2 or 4] to grab a high scale [scale 8] or vice versa. Then after using all your draw spells and searches, pendulum summon the two negates from your extra deck to Electrumite's zones and two negates from your hand that you drew into or searched. Then link into Selene and use Magister to summon back a negate you linked with (preferably Endymion) to get out 6 negates.\" Order is the whole trick: Electrumite EARLY, Pendulum Summon LATE, Selene LAST. [LC] agrees — \"The Pendulum Summon should take place as late as possible after all draws and searches have been conducted\" and \"Selene is usually made with Electrumite after the Pendulum Summon.\"\n\nWHICH SLOTS ACTUALLY MATTER [S]: \"The main priority cards you should prioritize in extra deck. Electromite, Seline, Ax code. Actually just those three are the main three that are the best. And then secondary... Crowley is only going to be in there. The next three you should probably prioritize would be uh Underworld Goddess, SP Little Knight.\"\n\n- **Heavymetalfoes Electrumite (2)** — Link-2 off 2 Pendulum Monsters. [S] ranks it #1: \"Electra is the top priority.\" MATERIALS [MDM]: \"it's ideal to first resolve Servant's effect to Special Summon herself and Jackal King or Endymion, and then use Servant and another Pendulum Monster as material. This lets you protect Electrumite from interruption.\" It does three things per summon: (1) on Link Summon, add a Pendulum from Deck to your Extra Deck FACE-UP — [S] calls this \"pull another negate from the deck\", i.e. bank a Jackal King or Endymion where Magister, Jackal King's Pendulum effect, Mythical Institution and your Pendulum Summon can all reach it; (2) once per turn destroy your own Pendulum-Zone card and add a face-up Extra Deck Pendulum to HAND — this is your scale fixer [S]: \"pop a low scale [scale 2 or 4] to grab a high scale [scale 8] or vice versa\"; (3) that same pop makes a card leave your Pendulum Zone, which draws 1. Blowing up your own scale is deliberate, not a cost you avoid. THEN Pendulum Summon into the two zones Electrumite points at, and only after that feed Electrumite to Selene.\n  PROTECT IT: [MDM] warns it \"is more vulnerable to interruption since you often need to use both Servant and Jackal King (summoned by her effect) as material.\" [S]'s answer is board a negate first — \"summon Jackal King so they can't negate Endymion (same going first when you're protecting Electrumite from handtraps)\"; [LC]: \"Summoning Jackal King early and leaving it on the field serves as a protection against many popular Handtraps for the rest of the Combo.\" An opponent on Shadow's guide video: \"I saved the imperm for electromy. I do. Now that's the rule.\"\n  WHY TWO: this copy count is a Master-Duel-only artifact — Electrumite is FORBIDDEN in the TCG and LIMITED to 1 in the OCG, so no TCG/OCG source has ever had reason to discuss a second. Mechanically the second copy is real: only the DRAW carries a hard once-per-turn-by-name clause, while the Link-Summon trigger has no once-per-turn at all and the destroy/retrieve is a plain per-copy \"Once per turn\". A second Electrumite therefore buys another Deck-to-face-up-Extra-Deck placement and another scale-fix-and-retrieve, but NEVER a second draw. [DATA]: 82/100 lists run 1 and 12/100 run 2 — and all twelve 2x lists are from 2026, Shadow's own among them. He has never stated the reason on record: the rationale above is mechanical, not quoted.\n\n- **Crowley, the First Propheseer (2)** — Link-2 off 2 Spellcaster monsters (any Spellcasters, unlike Electrumite which demands Pendulums — that is the whole reason both are here). On Link Summon: reveal 3 different-named 'Spellbook' cards from Deck, opponent randomly picks 1 for you. This deck contains EXACTLY three 'Spellbook' names — Spellbook Magician of Prophecy, Spellbook of Secrets, Spellbook of Knowledge. The Magician counts despite being a monster; Konami's ruling is explicit (Card Rulings:Crowley — \"Q: When revealing 3 'Spellbook' cards with the effect of 'Crowley, the First Propheseer', can I choose a 'Spellbook Magician of Prophecy'? A: Yes, you can.\"). So Crowley's search is LIVE ONLY WHILE ALL THREE ARE STILL IN THE DECK, which is exactly how players describe it [LC]: \"The usual Normal Summon is Spellbook Magician of Prophecy... If no Spellbook Card is drawn, then Link-2 Crowley can be Summoned with any two (preferably Special Summoned) Spellcasters to obtain one of the three Spellbook Cards.\" A YGOPRODeck Mythical Spellbook Endymion primer: \"You can also use crowley for the same thing, if you don't draw the right cards at the start.\"\n  [S] gives two reasons. It rescues an all-Pendulum hand: \"Konami loves to put only pendulums in the hand. This deck uses more spells than pendulums... I could actually go scale Servant Magister and pendulum summon the monsters from my hand, and then I can link them both away to Crowley... Crowley is what gives me the counters that I can confirm — confirmed counters.\" And it is a free draw-2 that does not cost your Normal Summon: \"Crowley is just free like 'oh I have two bodies' and turn that into a draw two... but you only really want to go for Crowley if you have not normal summoned.\" Another primer author frames it as a fork: \"Depending on the situation, I'll either go for Crowley or Electrumite.\"\n  WHEN NOT: make him BEFORE you Normal Summon the Magician or resolve Secrets — either removes a 'Spellbook' name from the Deck and the reveal needs all three still in there. Same reason Pot of Desires is a live risk: it banishes 10 face-down and can permanently kill Crowley's search by eating one of the three names. A primer author runs a 2-2-2 Spellbook package specifically to dodge this — \"I really like the possibility to always be able to go into Crowley and have its effect trigger even after Pot of Desires-ing\" — which this 1-1-1 build cannot do.\n  WHY TWO: no source, and the field says no. His search is a HARD once per turn BY NAME, so a second copy cannot search again that turn. [DATA]: 45/100 lists run Crowley and ZERO run 2 — Shadow's own list runs 1. Crowley's presence is 100% predicted by the Spellbook trio (45 of the 48 Spellbook lists run him; 0 of the 52 Spellbook-less lists do), i.e. he is played for the search and never as a generic body. Copy #2 is a spare Link-2 Spellcaster and nothing more.\n\n- **Artemis, the Magistus Moon Maiden (1)** — Link-1 off any Level 4 or lower Spellcaster (here: the Level-2 Spellbook Magician, or a Level-1 Mythical Beast Jackal). She exists for ONE job and all three sources name the same one. [MDM]: \"Artemis is only used along with Spellbook of Knowledge. Pendulum Monsters cannot be sent from the field to the GY, so Artemis converts any Level 4 or lower Pendulum Spellcaster into fodder for Knowledge.\" [S], unprompted: \"Artemis is there because if you draw Knowledge in your opening hand, you can still use Knowledge because you cannot use Knowledge on your Pendulums since they go to the Extra Deck and Knowledge has to send to the Graveyard. Artemis is there so you can normal summon a Pendulum, link it away for Artemis, and then draw two anyway.\" [LC] uses the identical unbrick: \"you can link off Timegazer into Artemis to be sent with Knowledge to draw 2, fixing an otherwise irreparable hand.\" The ruling underneath it (YGOrg QA #20866, quoted by [MDM]): \"If you attempt to send a Spellcaster Pendulum Monster you control to the GY with Spellbook of Knowledge, then it goes to the Extra Deck instead and you do NOT draw 2 cards.\" She also counts as a body for Crowley. Minor and unrecommended-by-anyone: she is a 'Magistus' card, so she is a legal cost for Magia Magic - Thunder of Judgment — but that Spell also lets you just pay 2 Spell Counters, which is nearly free here, so do not build around it. [DATA]: 49/100, never at 2.\n\n- **Linkuriboh (1)** — Link-1 off a Level 1 monster; in this deck that means Mythical Beast Jackal. [S] states the reason outright, and it is not the attack-stopper on the card: \"if you summon Jackal and get two counters, usually opponent will go 'Okay, I can Imperm negate the Jackal'... So if Jackal is negated, I don't have a way to get Jackal off the field. So Linkuriboh is there so I can [link it away].\" That is the slot: an Infinite Impermanence or Effect Veiler on your Level-1 Jackal otherwise leaves a dead body jamming a Monster Zone; Linkuriboh converts it into a Link body, frees the zone, and puts Jackal face-up in the Extra Deck where Jackal King's Pendulum effect can bring it back. WHEN NOT: it is not a combo piece — never spend Jackal on it while Jackal's own effect (remove 3 counters + Tribute itself, Special Summon a 'Mythical Beast' from Deck) is still live. [DATA]: 39/100, always 1. No written guide mentions it; [S] is the only source.\n\n- **Relinquished Anima (1)** — Link-1 off 1 Level 1 monster (Jackal again). [S]: \"Anima is there for the same way [as Linkuriboh] except he can out an opponent's monster, but it does lock off your Extra Monster Zone.\" Same escape hatch as Linkuriboh, upgraded to a steal — but her single arrow points UP, so she only reaches the opponent from an Extra Monster Zone, and that is precisely the zone [LC]'s endboard wants for Selene (\"A typical Endboard consists of Selene in the EMZ\"). Going second she is a free answer to one monster; going first, she and Selene are competing for the same square. [DATA]: 29/100, always 1, and declining in 2026. No Endymion guide names her — [S] is the only source.\n\n- **I:P Masquerena (1)** — Link-2 off 2 non-Link Monsters (any two spent Pendulum bodies), HELD to Link Summon during the opponent's Main Phase; whatever she makes cannot be destroyed by opponent card effects. [DATA]: 91/100 — the nearest thing to an auto-include here. [MDM] groups her with Magister and Selene: \"These 3 monsters each have Quick Effects that place additional interruptions on your field. Chain their effects directly to your last available negate, in order to ensure that you're always ready to negate your opponent's next effect before they have an opportunity to activate it.\" [S] also uses her to unclog zones so Magister can fire: \"we didn't have enough room to trigger Magister. Magister can summon another negate from the extra deck and himself can summon another negate during the opponent's turn... We freed more spots on our zones so we could go Magister to fill up the void with every single zone being negates.\" [S] on value: \"IP and SP are really good removal.\" WHEN NOT: never Link her away on your own turn — she is stored interruption.\n\n- **S:P Little Knight (1)** — Link-2 off 2 Effect Monsters, made from I:P on the opponent's turn. Because I:P is itself a Link Monster, S:P's clause \"If this card is Link Summoned using a Fusion, Synchro, Xyz, or Link Monster as material\" is met, so you banish 1 card on the field OR in either GY. Her second effect banishes 2 face-up monsters (one must be yours) until the End Phase — as much a dodge for your own boss as a disruption. [S] priority: \"The next three you should probably prioritize would be uh Underworld Goddess, SP Little Knight\" and \"IP and SP are really good removal.\" [DATA]: 77/100, and in a 2025-26 sample 31 of 32 S:P lists also ran I:P — they are one card in two halves. WHEN NOT: the on-summon banish stops your monsters attacking directly for the turn, so on your own turn while pushing for game, take the Quick Effect instead.\n\n- **Chaos Angel (1)** — Level 10 Synchro, 3500 ATK, in a deck with ZERO Tuners. It supplies its own: \"For this card's Synchro Summon, you can treat 1 LIGHT or DARK monster you control as a Tuner.\" [S] gives the exact pair: \"Basilisk removes three counters to summon out Jackal King from your hand. Now you got a level four Basilisk, got a level six Jackal King, a light and a dark, which means... Chaos Angel. So, essentially Basilisk makes summoning Chaos Angel very very easy.\" Checked against this engine: Mythical Beast Bashilisk is LIGHT Level 4, Mythical Beast Jackal King is DARK Level 6 — 4+6=10, and because you used one LIGHT and one DARK you collect BOTH bullets (Synchro Monsters you control unaffected by your opponent's activated monster effects, AND your monsters cannot be destroyed by battle) on top of the on-summon \"target 1 card on the field; banish it\".\n  The general rule, from Pojo's card reviews (Crunch$G): \"since any combination of LIGHT/DARK monsters whose Levels add to 10 makes this\" and \"literally any LIGHT/DARK strategy gets to run this without any issue.\" The both-bullets pattern is deliberate and widely known — r/masterduel: \"Both of Chaos Angel's effects can be active if you use both a light and a dark monster as material. Being a tuner, or being treated as a tuner doesn't matter in this case.\"\n  THE TRAP: 'a deck full of Spellcasters' is NOT the same as legal materials — the substitute-Tuner clause does NOT relax the requirement on the OTHER material, which must still be LIGHT or DARK (r/Yugioh101, on the identical mistake: \"If the Bystial is treated as a tuner, Ether Beryl is not a Light/Dark monster\"). Servant of Endymion is WIND. Magister of Endymion and Magical Abductor are EARTH. Spellbook Magician of Prophecy is WATER. None of them can be used at all. Your only legal bodies are DARK Endymion (Lv7) / Jackal King (Lv6) / Jackal (Lv1) and LIGHT Master Cerberus (Lv8) / Reflection (Lv7) / Bashilisk (Lv4) / Garuda (Lv4). Sums that hit exactly 10: Jackal King (6) + Bashilisk or Garuda (4) — the [S] line, and the one that gives both bullets; or Master Cerberus (8) + Jackal (1) + Jackal (1). Note that Endymion (7) and Reflection (7) are effectively STRANDED: the deck's only Level-3 monsters are Magister (EARTH) and Servant (WIND), so no 7+3 line exists.\n  TWO HOLES IN THE PROTECTION, both counter-intuitive: (a) the LIGHT bullet only stops MONSTER effects, and a Pendulum monster sitting in a Pendulum Zone is a SPELL, not a monster — so an opposing Endymion's scale effect (and every other Pendulum-Zone effect) goes straight through it; (b) if Chaos Angel ever leaves the field and is later revived rather than Synchro Summoned, it remembers nothing — Pojo: \"if Special Summoned back, Chaos Angel won't have any of these protections, making it a 3500 vanilla\" — though the banish still triggers, since that fires on any Special Summon.\n  WHEN: opportunistically, never as a goal. [S] is emphatic — \"it's a situational card that I guess if you have the opportunity to go for it, do it... you already have the combo line, so if it just presents itself, you have the room for it\", and \"Basti has a lot more utility outside of Chaos Angel, but I can just summon Chaos Angel whenever I need to.\" Bashilisk earns its main-deck slot on its own; never bend the line to reach the Synchro. Pojo's reviewers agree on the ceiling — \"while making it your main gameplan is ill-advised... it still has a banishing effect to help break boards\", with the listed con being \"No innate disruption on its own\". It is a board-breaker and a body, not an interruption.\n  [DATA]: 33/100 Endymion top decks, and Shadow has run exactly 1 in every list from January through July 2026 — the build is recognised by it (r/masterduel: \"There is a guy called shadow Spector. He's a twitch streamer and always play endymion. His version Is all links with a chaos angel and no beyond\"). Honest caveat: many of those 33 are repeat submissions of Shadow's own list, and Master Duel Meta's live deck breakdown puts Chaos Angel at 20% with trend 'down'.\n\n- **Selene, Queen of the Master Magicians (1)** — Link-3, 2+ monsters including a Spellcaster; standard materials are Electrumite plus one spare body, made AFTER the Pendulum Summon [LC]: \"Selene is usually made with Electrumite after the Pendulum Summon, sometimes even before it if that enables to Pend 3 from the FUED.\" [S] ranks her #2 and chose her over the Charmer Links: \"Selene is just easier to summon... I think Selene is just way more versatile.\" On Link Summon she banks Spell Counters equal to the number of Spells on the field AND IN BOTH GRAVEYARDS — with ~20 Spells maindecked that is a huge one-card bank. [MDM]: \"Selene instantly creates enough Spell Counters for any effect you might want to activate.\"\n  Because her Quick Effect and most costs read \"remove N Spell Counters from your FIELD\", her stack pays for Endymion's Pendulum wipe (6), Jackal King's negate (2), Master Cerberus's banish (4), Magister's monster effect (3) and Mythical Institution — but NOT for the Servant / Magister / Reflection PENDULUM effects, which say \"from THIS CARD\".\n  Her real payoff is recycling negates. [S] ends the line with her: \"Then link into Selene and use Magister to summon back a negate you linked with (preferably Endymion) to get out 6 negates.\" On the opponent's turn [LC]: Selene \"either revives Reflection or resummons a used up negate that was bounced by Endymion.\" [MDM] spells the loop out: \"1. Use Endymion's effect to negate a Spell/Trap, by returning to your hand a Jackal King or an Endymion that has already used its effect (or itself, if it has a Spell Counter). 2. Toggle your Chain response 'ON'. 3. Immediately after the Chain resolves, activate Selene's Quick Effect on a new Chain to Special Summon that same Jackal King or Endymion from your hand.\" And the chain-ordering trick [MDM]: \"Your opponent activates a Spell/Trap and you Chain with your only copy of Endymion as Chain Link 2. Activate Selene's effect as Chain Link 3. When the Chain resolves, Selene Special Summons a second Endymion from your hand or GY, and then the previous Endymion negates your opponent's Spell/Trap.\"\n  GOTCHAS: her Quick Effect is MAIN PHASE ONLY; she revives in DEFENCE Position (bad for Endymion and Jackal King, whose DEF is low); the untargetable-by-attacks clause only applies while an 'Endymion' card is on the field; and she can NEVER be Endymion's bounce fodder — a Link Monster goes to the Extra Deck, not the hand, and [MDM, YGOrg QA #22525] \"If Endymion's Quick Effect does not return a card with a Spell Counter to the hand... it does not negate the Spell/Trap activation.\"\n  ON THE COUNT: both her effects are SOFT once per turn, and [LC] says \"Selene can be used more than once per turn. Sometimes, all three can be needed in one turn.\" [DATA]: 39/100 lists run 2 (a couple run 3). This list runs 1 — as does Shadow's.\n\n- **Knightmare Unicorn (1)** — Link-3, 2+ monsters with different names; discard 1, then shuffle any 1 card on the field into the DECK (beats graveyard recursion and banish-dodgers in a way S:P does not). [S] gives the exact use, and it is the counter-intuitive bit — the discard is free here because Endymion's negate hands you a card: \"you want to use a Demian [Endymion] to bounce a card in the hand that has a counter. You want to use another Endymion to bounce the card that already negated... Then you want to go I:P Masquerena to link with that monster you negated with into Unicorn to discard whatever you just returned to the hand.\" [S] also treats it as a swap for S:P: \"if you have unicorn, you don't have SP.\" HONESTY: this is a fringe slot. [DATA]: 8/100 overall and 1/40 in a 2025-26-only sample; Master Duel Meta's card database lists it as played in no Master Duel deck type; Shadow's own list does not run it. Keep it only if you specifically want deck-shuffling over banishing.\n\n- **Underworld Goddess of the Closed World (1)** — Link-5 off 4+ Effect Monsters, and it may use 1 of the OPPONENT'S monsters as material. This is the going-second answer to a monster nothing else beats. [MDM] files it under 'Removing an Unaffected Monster': \"An Endymion deck usually has no problem fielding enough materials for Underworld Goddess\", and \"of course, Underworld Goddess will always get rid of an opponent's monster if nothing else will.\" [S] names it in his anti-Towers package — \"can you out two towers? I can yes I can do it with a maxax [Avramax] and axis code [Accesscode] and underworld goddess\" — and puts it in his second priority tier. On summon it negates every face-up monster the opponent controls, and afterwards it is unaffected by their activated effects unless they target it. [DATA]: 62/100. WHEN NOT: four of your own bodies is your entire going-first board — this is a turn-2 card.\n\n- **Accesscode Talker (1)** — Link-4, [S]'s #3 priority. A going-second / OTK card, not an endboard piece. [LC]: \"Selene in turn usually yields a free Accesscode Talker... and usually two pops.\" (Check the arithmetic yourself: 2300 + a Link-3 Selene's rating x 1000 = 5300 ATK, not the 5800 that guide prints.) Your opponent cannot respond to its effects at all. The pops are Attribute-locked — each Link Monster you banish locks out that Attribute for the rest of the turn — so your pop count equals the number of DISTINCT Link Attributes you can bank. In this Extra Deck: Electrumite is FIRE; Selene, Artemis and Underworld Goddess are LIGHT; Crowley, Relinquished Anima, Linkuriboh, I:P, S:P and Knightmare Unicorn are DARK. Electrumite -> Selene -> any DARK is the natural three-pop chain. WHEN NOT: going first, spend the bodies on negates — [LC]'s deckbuilding rule is \"Winmore cards are unnecessary. The Deck already has a great ceiling.\"\n\n- **Apollousa, Bow of the Goddess (1)** — READ BEFORE PLAYING. Apollousa is FORBIDDEN in the TCG, the OCG *and* Master Duel (verified against both Master Duel Meta's and YGOPRODeck's card databases). This engine enforces no banlist so the card functions here, but no real Endymion pilot has been able to build it since the hit: 0/40 Endymion top decks in an October-2025-to-August-2026 sample run it, and Shadow's list does not. The only sourced role predates the ban — [LC] listed it among \"disruptions on the opponent's turn... Apollousa, Bow of the Goddess (monster effects)\", made under Selene, typically off I:P. Its original ATK is 800 x materials and each negate costs exactly 800, so 4 differently-named materials gives 3200 ATK and 4 negates. UNSOURCED for any modern build. The cards real 2026 lists put in this slot instead are Mekk-Knight Crusadia Avramax and the Charmer Links.\n\nWHAT THE SOURCE LIST ACTUALLY RAN: Shadow Spector's January 2026 Extra Deck, recovered in full from Master Duel Meta's API, is 2x Heavymetalfoes Electrumite, 1x Crowley, 1x Artemis, 1x Relinquished Anima, 1x Linkuriboh, 1x I:P Masquerena, 1x Chaos Angel, 1x Selene, 1x S:P Little Knight, 1x Accesscode Talker, 1x Underworld Goddess, 1x Lyna the Light Charmer Lustrous, 1x Dharc the Dark Charmer Gloomy, 1x Mekk-Knight Crusadia Avramax. This build differs in exactly three slots: the 2nd Crowley, Knightmare Unicorn and Apollousa stand in for Lyna, Dharc and Avramax. Of those three substitutes only Knightmare Unicorn has a stated use; the 2nd Crowley is dead weight and Apollousa is illegal everywhere real.\n\n=== GOING SECOND ===\nYou are a strong turn-2 deck. **Triple Tactics Talent** (after the opponent uses a monster effect on your turn) draws 2, steals a monster, or peeks-and-shuffles. Dig with Pot of Desires / Upstart / Into the Void, load counters, then use **Endymion's Pendulum effect as a board wipe** (destroy up to N cards after stacking counter-holders), **Master Cerberus** and **Magia Magic** to banish, **Reflection / Garuda** to bounce, and **Underworld Goddess of the Closed World** (Link-5, uses an opponent's monster as material and negates on summon) or **Knightmare Unicorn** to punch through, finishing with **Accesscode Talker**.\n\n=== HANDTRAP NAVIGATION ===\n- **Called by the Grave (1)** answers Ash Blossom / Maxx \"C\" / Nibiru by banishing + negating the same-named effect.\n- **Ash Blossom** on Spell Power Mastery or a Spellbook: you have redundancy (3x Mastery + Institution + Abductor + Servant/Jackal tutors) — eat it and continue with a different starter.\n- **Maxx \"C\":** keep the line SHORT (Electrumite + one negate) or turn it around with Triple Tactics; don't over-extend into a free draw engine.\n- **Nibiru, the Primal Being:** count your Special Summons — Endymion floods fast. Stop at 4 summons if Nibiru is live, or bait it; Endymion / Master Cerberus is your post-Nibiru beater and can rebuild off banked counters and cards face-up in the Extra Deck.\n- **Droll & Lock Bird:** shuts the search engine — pivot to Pendulum Summoning the monsters already in hand and to Endymion's Pendulum wipe, which need no searching.\n\n=== WEAKNESSES ===\n- **Anti-Spell floodgates are lethal:** Anti-Spell Fragrance / Mystic Mine stop your Spells, which stops counters, which stops the entire engine. These are your worst matchup.\n- **Droll & Lock Bird** cripples the cantrip/search chain.\n- **Bounce/banish removal** (Evenly Matched, Lightning Storm, Forbidding, Kaijus) sidesteps Citadel/Institution, which only redirect DESTRUCTION.\n- **Bricking:** hands of only high-scale pendulums with no starter stall you — but 3x Spell Power Mastery, Magical Abductor, Mythical Institution, and the Servant/Jackal tutors keep the starter count high.\n- The board leans on counters; a first-Spell negate or a well-timed disruption before you bank counters slows the whole turn.",
  "main": [
